t-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>I increased the grain bill by 75% trying to achieve a 45llt yield. Ended up with a 1065og. Can&#039;t drink too much of this bad boy and expect to get up in the morning! Will brew again but pay more attention to my brew house efficiency</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR><table class="bf_recipe_comment" with="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td width="50" valign="top"><center><img style="max-width:48px;max-height:48px;border-radius: 3px;" src="//www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/images/brewersfriendlogo.png" alt="Brewer's Friend Logo"></td><td width=7></td><td valign='top'><a href='https://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/brewer/398647'><font style='font-weight:700;color:#777;font-size:13px;line-height:1;'>SirQueuesalot</font></a><font style='color: rgba(0, 39, 59, 0.35);font-size: 12px;font-weight: 500;'> <font style='font-size:9.75px;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif;line-height:13.65px;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;padding-left:4px;padding-right:4px;'>&bull;</font> 10/13/2025 at 10:54am</font><BR><font style='line-height:21px;font-style: normal;font-weight:400;font-family: Helvetica Neue,arial,sans-serif; color: #3f4549;font-size:15px;'>Having so much fun with this recipe trying to dial in brewhouse efficiency, it&#039;s an outstanding recipe that hasn&#039;t failed to delight irrespective of the strength I&#039;m producing.</font><BR></td></tr></table><BR><bR></td></tr></table></div><div style='clear:both;'></div>
	

	
